# Chief visual approval

This site is edited by a cloud agent prompted by Grok. The chief approves
user-visible changes only from screenshot and video proof.

## After any visible change

1. Serve locally with `python3 -m http.server 5174` and open `http://127.0.0.1:5174`.
2. Exercise the changed flow as a visitor (click, type, filter, open lightbox, submit).
3. Capture after screenshots of every affected section. Include mobile (390px) when
   layout or navigation changed.
4. Record a video of the working flow with `RecordScreen` + `computerUse`.
   Launch `computerUse` and `videoReview` on a **Grok** model only (`inherit`
   or `cursor-grok-4.6-*`). Never Claude, GPT, Gemini, Composer, or Muse.
   Discard failed takes; do not upload a broken walkthrough.
5. Copy screenshots to `/opt/cursor/artifacts` using snake_case names.
6. Run `videoReview` on Grok before citing the video.
7. Embed the artifacts in the PR and the final message. Ask the chief to approve
   from that proof.

## Never

- Ask for approval from a text description alone.
- Deploy to Hostinger / production until the chief explicitly approves.
- Upload screenshots or videos of failing tests.
- Use Claude, GPT, Gemini, Composer, Muse, or any non-Grok model for
  screenshots, recordings, reviews, or any other work.
